WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.301
Operational technology, usually shortened to OT,

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:07.436
is the collection of hardware and software used to monitor or control physical processes.

00:00:07.436 --> 00:00:11.103
OT reads conditions in the real world, makes control decisions,

00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:12.937
and causes equipment to act.

00:00:12.937 --> 00:00:16.238
A temperature sensor, a controller that opens a valve,

00:00:16.238 --> 00:00:20.640
and the workstation that shows an operator the process state can all

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.840
belong to the same OT environment.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.508
OT is present wherever digital systems interact with physical operations.

00:00:26.508 --> 00:00:30.543
Manufacturing plants use it to run production lines and industrial robots.

00:00:30.543 --> 00:00:34.211
Electric utilities use it to monitor substations and balance power.

00:00:34.211 --> 00:00:37.512
Water facilities control pumps, treatment stages, and chemical dosing.

00:00:37.512 --> 00:00:39.712
Transportation systems manage signaling and traffic.

00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:42.280
Building automation controls heating, ventilation, access, lighting,

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.747
and life-safety support systems.

00:00:43.747 --> 00:00:47.415
This physical connection distinguishes OT from a conventional information system.

00:00:47.415 --> 00:00:50.716
A business application primarily stores, processes, or communicates data.

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:53.283
An OT system may do those things,

00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:56.218
but its purpose is to influence a process.

00:00:56.218 --> 00:01:00.252
Incorrect data in an office report can cause a business problem.

00:01:00.252 --> 00:01:04.287
An incorrect control value can stop machinery, damage equipment, release material,

00:01:04.287 --> 00:01:05.754
or create unsafe conditions.

00:01:05.754 --> 00:01:07.955
OT environments are therefore cyber-physical systems.

00:01:07.955 --> 00:01:10.155
Digital components, networks, software, operators, machinery,

00:01:10.155 --> 00:01:13.090
and the underlying process must be considered together.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.591
Security cannot be evaluated solely by looking at an operating system version or firewall rule.

00:01:18.591 --> 00:01:22.626
Analysts must understand what the system controls, how operators use it,

00:01:22.626 --> 00:01:24.093
what safe operation requires,

00:01:24.093 --> 00:01:27.761
and what happens when communications or control functions are disrupted.

00:01:27.761 --> 00:01:31.062
OT security protects the dependable operation of these systems.

00:01:31.062 --> 00:01:33.996
That includes preventing unauthorized changes, detecting abnormal behavior,

00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:37.297
preserving reliable visibility for operators, and supporting safe recovery.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:40.965
The central question is not only, “Is the data protected?

00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:45.733
” It is also, “Can the physical operation continue safely and as intended?

00:01:45.733 --> 00:01:46.100
”
